 "text": "Reference\nAAR 2023\nAudit Observations\n4. Out of 222 Gender and Development (GAD)\nObservation No. 4 Programs/Projects/Activitles (PPAs), 22 were\nPage 90\nunimplemented and 84 were not reported in the\nGAD Accomplishment Report (AR) or have no\nstatus contrary to. RA No. 9710 Thus, the City's\nobjective of ensuring awareness and sustaining\nsupport for gender and development, women's\nempowerment and response to gender issues\nwere not fully realized.\nAudit Recommendations\nWe recommended that Management\ndirectinstruct the GFPS to:\n4.12.1. Regularly monitor and evaluate the\nutilization of the GPB to ensure that PPAs are\nfully Implemented as planned and challenges\nthat cause non-Implementation, if any, are\nIdentified and addressed;\nAAR 2023\n5. A total of P472.416 million withheld for CY\nObservation No. 5 2023 remittances to the BIR, GSIS, Pag-IBIG and\nPage 93\nPhilHealth have not been remitted by the City\ncontrary to existing rules and regulations.\n4.12.2. Ensure that only PPAs listed In the\napproved GPB will be charged against the\nGAD Fund; and\n4.12.3. Comply with the provisions of the\nJMCs discussed and RA No. 9710 and Its IRR.\n5.11. We recommended and Management\nagreed to ensure prompt and full remittance\nof all withholding taxes, contributions,\npremlum payments, loan amortization and\nother amounts due to the BIR, GSIS, Pag-IBIG\nand PhilHealth pursuant to the above-\nmentioned regulations.\nAGENCY ACTION PLAN\nPerson/Dept.\nTarget Implementation Date\nAction Plan\nStatus of\nImplementation\nResponsible\nFrom\nTo\nReason for Partial/Delsy/\nNon-Implementation, if\napplicable\nOffice of the City\nMayor\n2024\n2024 Ongoing\nAction Taken/Action to\nbe Taken\nThe GFPS directed the\nGAD Focal Persons to\ncarry over the\nunimplemented 2023\nPPAs to the 2024 GAD\nPPAs. As a remedlal\nmeasure for the\nunimplemented CAP\nDEV or Trainings on\nGAD, the City Personnel\nOffice would be\nconducting Seminar-\nWorkshop on GAD\nMainstreaming on\nSeptember 16-17,2024\nwhich would be\nparticipated by\nomployees/representat!\nves from the 44\nDepartments. Further,\nIn our 3rd and 4th GAD\nTWG Meetings we\nIncluded in the Agenda\nGAD Planning &\nBudgeting to empower\nthe newly appointed\nGAD Focal Persons to\nSee above\nOffice of the City\nMayor\n2024\n2024 Ongoing\nOffice of the City\nMayor\n2024\n2024 Ongoing\nSee above\nOCAT and CTO\n2024\n2024 Ongoing\nIssues related to\nemployees detalls and\nThe OCAT In\nInformation (for Clarif\nItems) for GSIS, On the\nother hand the amount\ncoordination with CTO\nremitting the remaining\nunremitted amount to\npayable to BIR reflects the date.\nwithholding taxes related\nto unpald payable to\ndifferent suppliers.\nIs continuously\n",
